9s3","text":"eb` for your profile if\nyou run another one."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| **`/store`** | Opens the catalogue over the session — search by capability, see what each plugin r"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"eaches, install without leaving the harness. |\n| **Install-tested only** | Every plugin offered here"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" already installed cleanly in a throwaway sandbox. Anything that failed, needs a manual build-script"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" approval, or was never tested stays off the shelf — the full catalogue, verdicts included, is on ds"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"hmarketplace.dev. |\n| **Settings tab** | The same catalogue, docked under Settings → Plugins. |\n| **"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"Agent tools** | `dshmarketplace_search` and `dshmarketplace_install`, so *\"find me a memory plugin a"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"nd set it up\"* works in conversation. |\n| **Bundled skill** | Teaches the agent to search rather tha"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"n recall a plugin name from training data — for an ecosystem this young, a remembered name is usuall"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"y wrong. |\n| **Bilingual** | Every listing carries a hand-written English and Chinese description. T"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"he plugin follows your DSH language setting, live. |\n| **Discover tab** | On DSH 0.2.1-rc.2+, adds o"},{"id":"p11s11","text":"ur plugin index to **Plugins → Discover**. Every entry is a release our sandbox installed, labelled "},{"id":"p11s12","text":"with the dsh version it installed on (and, once checked, whether the next `next` / `alpha` release a"},{"id":"p11s13","text":"ccepts it), sortable by recommended, stars this week, stars and installs. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### The Discover index"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"DSH 0.2.1-rc.2 added an experimental **Custom plugin indexes** bundle (Plugins →\nExperimental plugin"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"s) that browses third-party indexes in a **Discover** tab.\nOnce per profile, the plugin switches tha"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"t bundle on and appends\n`https://dshmarketplace.dev/market/index.json` after any sources you already"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"\nhave. It never adds the source twice and never touches your other sources. If\nyou switch the bundle"},{"id":"p13s5","text":" off or remove the source, it stays that way — run\n`/store-index` to put both back. On a DSH without"},{"id":"p13s6","text":" the bundle (0.2.0 and 0.1),\nnothing happens and `/store-index` says why."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Safety"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Plugins run with your agent's permissions, and a listing is not a security\nreview. Three things this"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" plugin does about that."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"**Install commands are validated, never interpolated.** The catalogue supplies a\ncommand already bui"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"lt; `src/installer.js` accepts only a bare npm specifier or\n`github:owner/repo`, refuses anything co"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ntaining `..`, and passes arguments as an\narray rather than through a shell. If the catalogue were e"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ver compromised, the\nblast radius stops there. `tests/installer.test.js` covers that boundary\nspecif"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"ically — writing it found a real hole, since `../../etc/passwd` is only\nword characters, dots and sl"},{"id":"p16s6","text":" — writing it found a real hole, since `../../etc/passwd` is only\nword characters, dots and slashes."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**The browser half cannot reach the shell.** It talks to two exact-path local\nendpoints, and the ins"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"tall endpoint takes a catalogue entry rather than a\ncommand, so the client cannot widen what runs."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"**Risk flags gate both paths.** Listings carry detected `install script`,\n`terminal surface` and `re"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"quires credentials` flags. Anything flagged stops for\nan explicit confirmation, in the UI and on the"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" agent path alike — and the\nconfirmation says plainly that an empty list would not have meant it was"},{"id":"p18s4","text":" path alike — and the\nconfirmation says plainly that an empty list would not have meant it was safe."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Privacy"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The plugin sends exactly one thing anywhere: after a successful install, the\nplugin's public identif"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ier, so install counts are real. No machine id, no\nsession id, no user, no query, no telemetry of an"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"y other kind. Searches go to\nthe public catalogue API in order to answer them and carry no identifie"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"rs.\nThe Discover index is fetched by DSH itself, not by this plugin; the plugin\nonly keeps a small m"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"arker, `.dshmarketplace-plugin.json`, in the profile\ndirectory so it adds the source once."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The browser bundle may only require `react` and\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives`, and must an"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"nounce itself through\n`window.__ModuleLoader__.load`. `build.mjs` enforces both against the emitted\n"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"code before writing it, so an unsupported import fails here instead of inside\nsomeone else's harness"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ode before writing it, so an unsupported import fails here instead of inside\nsomeone else's harness."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Related"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- DeepSeekV5.dev — independent bilingual model\nguides, API pricing and a browser-based cost calculat"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"or\n- dshmarketplace.dev — the catalogue, with a\nwritten page per plugin\n- `dshmarketplace-cli` —\nthe"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" same catalogue for coding agents outside DSH\n- `GET /api/v1/plugins` — the public API all three rea"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"same catalogue for coding agents outside DSH\n- `GET /api/v1/plugins` — the public API all three read"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Contact"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Community** — LINUX DO\n- **Issues** — GitHub Issues"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"MIT. Independent project, not affiliated with DeepSeek. DeepSeek and DeepSeek\nHarness are marks of t"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"heir respective owner, used here only to describe what\nthis plugin is for."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

